      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually this is a bad use of iota.\n\niota should not be used when the numbers must have explicit values as expected by others (e.g. RFC 5280)\n\nThe RFC says:\n\n\n   CRLReason ::\u003d ENUMERATED {\n        unspecified             (0),\n        keyCompromise           (1),\n        cACompromise            (2),\n        affiliationChanged      (3),\n        superseded              (4),\n        cessationOfOperation    (5),\n        certificateHold         (6),\n             -- value 7 is not used\n        removeFromCRL           (8),\n        privilegeWithdrawn      (9),\n        aACompromise           (10) }\n\n\nSo, please replace iota here with explicit numbers.",
